course: dictionary
lesson: 1345
title: Camping words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Camping means staying outdoors in a tent or a camper van for fun. The word camping can be a noun, as in «camping gear», or the -ing form of the verb camp, as in «We are camping». You can usually tell which by the words around it.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means. «On a camping trip, far from city lights, the sky is full of stars and you feel tiny.» The words far from city lights tell you the trip is outdoors, away from towns, so the sky looks full of stars.
explain: Camping trips are not only fun. «Picture a camping trip with no tent from a shop, no matches and no supermarket» shows that a camper must plan carefully. You must know which berries are safe, where the deer drink and how to keep a fire alive.
fact: Camping means staying outdoors in a tent or a camper van for fun.
fact: Camping is also the -ing form of the verb camp, as in «We are camping».
fact: A campsite is a place where people set up tents or camper vans.
fact: Camping gear means the things you take with you, such as a tent, mats and warm layers.
fact: On a cold camping night, the ground pulls heat out of your body faster than the air does, so people sleep on foam mats and wear hats and dry layers.
exercise: «On a camping trip, far from city lights, the sky is full of stars.» Where would you be on this trip? | At school in a classroom | In a shop buying a tent | In a city full of street lamps | *Outdoors, far away from towns and city lights
exercise: Ben says, «We are camping this weekend.» What does camp mean here? | To pack a suitcase for a holiday abroad | *To stay outdoors in a tent for fun | To swim in the sea | To climb a tall hill
exercise: «Picture a camping trip with no tent from a shop, no matches and no supermarket.» Find and copy the word that means a shop selling food. | *supermarket | tent | camping | matches
test: Which word names a place where people set up tents for a camping trip? | *campsite | cold ground | camping gear | foam mat
test: What do you call the things you pack for a camping trip, such as a tent, mats and warm layers? | campsite | camping night | deer | *camping gear
exam: Which sentence shows that camping means staying outdoors for fun? | Mum cooked dinner in the kitchen. | Tom went to the shop to buy milk and bread. | *On a camping trip, far from city lights, the sky is full of stars and you feel tiny. | The school bus was late again this morning.
